**Claim 1.** A process for manufacturing a composite sheet comprising a lower metal cover layer, an upper metal cover layer, and a plastic core layer integrally bonded between the lower and upper metal cover layers, the process comprising:

providing the lower and upper metal cover layers with respective inwardly facing bonding surfaces;

disposing a plastic core material between the respective bonding surfaces;

heating the plastic core material to a bond-forming state;

bringing the lower and upper metal cover layers and the plastic core material together under pressure to form a continuous laminate in which the plastic core material contacts and bonds to the respective bonding surfaces; and

cooling the laminate while maintaining the lower and upper metal cover layers in spaced relation, thereby solidifying the plastic core material and producing the composite sheet with the plastic core layer integrally bonded to both metal cover layers.
